cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use PyPottery in your research, please cite the software and, for each
  module you used, the article listed under references.
type: software
title: "PyPottery Suite: Digitizing Archaeological Pottery Documentation"
abstract: >-
  PyPottery is a suite of five open-source tools (PyPotteryLens, PyPotteryScan,
  PyPotteryInk, PyPotteryTrace and PyPotteryLayout) that automate the classical
  archaeological pottery documentation workflow: extracting figures from
  monograph PDFs, digitizing field cards, inking pencil drawings, vectorizing
  vessel profiles and composing publication plates. Everything runs locally.
authors:
